ncient ramparts still mark the border of the city and the beginning of a natural reserve area.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"'s-Hertogenbosch","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/%27s-Hertogenbosch","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Den Bosch, properly 's-Hertogenbosch, is a cathedral city in the Netherlands with a reputation for food. The Citadel and Kamp Vught are the sober stops; ten hours suits the centre, and May to September is the comfortable run.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":160783,"visit_h":9.6}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-vught","name":"Vught","kind":"Landmark","lat":51.65559,"lon":5.29212,"dist_km":3.1,"sig":2.483,"rank_score":10.58,"resolved_by":"retyped","fact":"Town and municipality in North Brabant, Netherlands","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Vught%2C_kerk1_foto4_2011-05-30_13.35.JPG/960px-Vught%2C_kerk1_foto4_2011-05-30_13.35.JPG","author":"Michielverbeek","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vught,_kerk1_foto4_2011-05-30_13.35.JPG","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vught","heritage":true},{"id":"hl-kamp-vught","name":"Kamp Vught","kind":"Landmark","lat":51.66724,"lon":5.25904,"dist_km":3.3,"sig":1.306,"rank_score":9.13,"resolved_by":"retyped","fact":"Nazi concentration camp in the Netherlands (1943-1945)","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herzogenbusch_concentration_camp","merged_from":["Kindermonument Kamp Vught","Nationaal Monument Kamp Vught"]},{"id":"hl-brabanthallen","name":"Brabanthallen","kind":"Landmark","lat":51.70111,"lon":5.28972,"dist_km":2.1,"sig":2.864,"rank_score":8.79,"resolved_by":"retyped","fact":"Convention center in The Netherlands","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/522513_Congrescentrum_Brabanthallen.jpg/960px-522513_Congrescentrum_Brabanthallen.jpg","author":"Johan Bakker","licence"